# Business Recommendations

### 1. Improve Initial Applicant Screening

The largest funnel drop-off occurs between Application and Screening, with **72.30% of applicants not progressing**.
Standardize screening criteria and consider automated initial filtering to improve candidate quality and reduce 
manual screening workload.

### 2. Prioritize High-Performing Sourcing Channels

Employee Referral has the highest hire rate at **5.94%**.
Recruitment teams should evaluate opportunities to strengthen employee referral programs while reviewing the 
cost-effectiveness of recruitment agencies before increasing investment.

### 3. Investigate High-Cost Departments

Operations has the highest average cost per hire at **€4,082.12**.
The recruitment team should review sourcing channels, recruitment processes and hiring activities within 
Operations to identify opportunities to reduce cost per successful hire.

### 4. Scale Recruiter Best Practices

Michael Wagner demonstrates strong performance across conversion, speed and cost.
The recruitment team could identify the practices contributing to this performance and determine whether 
they can be standardized or shared across the wider recruiting team.

